          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A concert venue charges $50 per ticket and incurs a fixed cost of $2000 to host an event. Each attendee costs an additional $10 in expenses.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p34-q43-task",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Write equations for revenue and cost, and determine how many tickets must be sold to break even.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For $x$ tickets, $R(x)=50x$ and $C(x)=2000+10x$, in dollars.\n\nBreak-even: 50 tickets.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number of tickets sold. Revenue and cost are in dollars.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}R(x)&=50x\\\\C(x)&=2000+10x\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt break-even, $R(x)=C(x)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}50x&=2000+10x\\\\40x&=2000\\\\x&=50\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, 50 tickets must be sold.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
